# Ozikoro Store — environment
#
# NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS A REAL SECRET. It lists what the application reads, so
# a deployment does not fail at two in the morning because a variable was missed.
#
# Secrets are set with `wrangler secret put` and never committed:
#   npx wrangler secret put PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY
#
# There is no session-signing key to configure. The session cookie is 256 bits
# of randomness and the database stores only its SHA-256, so a stolen dump is not
# a set of working sessions and there is nothing to sign.
#
# Non-secret configuration lives in vite.config.ts under
# `nitro.cloudflare.wrangler.vars`, which Nitro writes into the deployed
# wrangler.json. These variables are read through `src/lib/env.ts`.

# --- bindings (declared in vite.config.ts, present in wrangler dev) ---------
# DB            D1 database, name `ozikoro-store`
# STORE_CACHE   optional KV namespace for hot catalogue reads

# --- non-secret vars --------------------------------------------------------
STORE_ENV=production
STORE_ORIGIN=https://shop.ozikoro.com
# A record of who owns the store. It is NOT an authorisation list: admin access
# is a role on the account, granted by a super admin, because an environment
# variable that grants access is one leaked value away from a takeover.
STORE_ADMIN_EMAILS=hello@ozikoro.com

# --- secrets (wrangler secret put, never here) ------------------------------
# PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY   sk_test_… or sk_live_…  (required for checkout)
# ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN optional; reserved for an owner-only diagnostic surface

# --- build-time only --------------------------------------------------------
# The D1 database id, so a build can target a database other than production.
# STORE_D1_DATABASE_ID=b4111199-9dfb-4f85-bdd1-eff593afcb15
